# Hosts that must reach the internet DIRECTLY while Brave runs through Hiddify.
# Read by ~/.local/bin/brave-hiddify and handed to Brave as --proxy-bypass-list.
# One rule per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#
# Chromium matches a rule against the host in the URL, so "example.com" covers
# the apex domain and "*.example.com" covers only its subdomains - list BOTH
# when you want the apex domain included (verified on Brave snap 690).
#
# Verified-working syntax: <local>, example.com, example.com:80,
# *.example.com, 192.168.*, 192.168.0.0/16, and comma-separated lists.

# This machine, localhost, *.local. Chromium already bypasses these by default.
<local>

# Local network - a remote proxy can never reach the router, NAS or a printer.
192.168.*
10.*
172.16.*

# Russian sites that reject or throttle foreign IPs (banks, some services).
# Uncomment per domain, apex + wildcard as above.
#example.ru
#*.example.ru
